media: qcom: camss: add SM8450 support (Tab S8+ camera stage 1)

Adds the qcom,sm8450-camss compatible, its resource tables, a binding and
the camss node in sm8450.dtsi. ADR-001 chose the mainline CAMSS raw path
for the SM-X800 cameras (docs/architecture/001-camera-stack-mainline-camss.md,
issue #27).

The SM8450 blocks are csiphy-v2.1.0, csid680 x3 + csid-lite680 x2 and
vfe680 x3 + vfe-lite680 x2. Mainline 7.2 already drives csid680 and vfe680
through csid_ops_680 / vfe_ops_680 (used by the X1E80100 tables), and the
X1E80100 csiphy lane table is the downstream csiphy_2ph_v2_1_0_reg table
entry for entry with the DNP writes dropped, common block at 0x1000. So
CAMSS_8450 joins the X1E80100 arm in csiphy_init and reuses both 680 ops.
vfe_ops_gen3 is wrong here: it addresses RDI0 as bus write master 23 (VFE
780); vfe680 RDI0-2 are clients 24-26.

Values come from the stock SM-X800 DTB and camcc-sm8450: registers, edge
interrupts, clock rates (csid/cphy_rx 400/480 MHz, ife 432/594/675/727 MHz),
IFE_0/1/2 and TITAN_TOP GDSCs, apps_smmu SIDs 0x800 mask 0x460, CSIPHY
rails L5B 0.88 V (147 mA) and L6B 1.2 V (59.4 mA). Stock camcc indices equal
the mainline header values. vfe_lite windows follow the sm8550 layout at
csid_lite + 0x1000, which matches the downstream vfe_lite68x offsets (+0x1000
from the ife-lite node base). Full VFEs get line_num 3: vfe680 has RDI0-2
and line 3 would register the unsupported PIX path on write master 27.

Not modelled, as on every other SoC in mainline: camnoc QoS, CPAS qchannel
handshake, TPG. Register comparison against the Samsung GPL 5.10 techpack
(akm-04/Samsung_Kernel_sm8450_common_gts8x, 04d43557ead2) is recorded in
issue #27.

